"i18n.vaccineapp.TnC"="<h3>Privacy Policy and General Terms and Conditions </h3>                                                       <p id=\"Privacy_Policy\">Please read the Privacy Policy and General Terms and Conditions governing the International Organization for Migration Vaccine App (“the application”). By clicking “I Agree” below, you are entering into a legally binding agreement with the International Organization for Migration (IOM)   <p>   <h3>1. PRIVACY POLICY </h3> <p>IOM seeks to ensure that any personal information processed through the application is handled with the utmost care and confidentiality. Data privacy is a human right and is essential to human dignity.<br></br>     This Privacy Policy, as integral part of the General Terms and Conditions, explains how IOM collects, registers, stores, uses, shares or otherwise processes your information on this application. By accessing and using this application, you agree to the terms in this Privacy Policy. <br></br>   IMPORTANT NOTICE: You must be over 18 to use the application. If you are under 18, your parents or legal guardians must be the ones to access and accompany you through the site specifically provided in the application.</p>  <h3>Who are we?</h3> <p>IOM is a United Nations related organization working on migration issues. IOM works to help ensure the orderly and human management of migration for the benefit of all. It does so by providing services and advice to governments and migrants.</p>  <h3>Why are we collecting personal data about you?</h3> <p>IOM processes your personal data to register your profile in the application. By doing so, you agree that IOM creates your personal digital health space that allows you to access your health information, consult appointments and carry out procedures in a simple, secure and confidential way.</p>  <h3>What personal data are we collecting?</h3> <p> When you register your profile, you agree that the following mandatory fields with your personal data are recorded in the application: email address, phone number, last name, first name, middle name, date of birth, relationship, and country of location. <br></br>     You will have an opportunity to confirm your personal data until you enroll your device in the application. Thus, you certify that any information you provide through the application, is true, accurate and up to date.<br></br>   You agree to maintain the security of your profile and not sharing the details to any third party.</p>  <h3>Which data contains your profile? </h3> <p> Upon your confirmation, the relevant data related to your health status and/or of your dependents processed by IOM through the Health Assessments processes will be uploaded and accessible in the application.</p>  <h3>For what purpose was your data collected?</h3>  <p>The purpose of this application is to provide IOM beneficiaries with a platform to access their health information, consult appointments and carry out procedures in a simple, secure and confidential way.<br></br>   Your personal data was collected and stored in the IOM’s database for the purpose of providing you with vaccination information, notifications, certificates, health education by one of IOM’s Migration Health Assessment Centers.<br></br>   Data of your accesses and use of the application would be de-identified by removing your personal information if they need to be used for research such as analysis of migration health issues to inform policy or programme evaluation to improve the service.<br></br>     IOM will not sell or rent personal data collected through the application.   <h3>What security measures are taken to safeguard your information </h3> <p>Any personal data collected, received, used, transferred, stored or otherwise processed by IOM are protected by strict conditions of confidentiality and security, in line with the IOM Data Protection Principles:<a href=\"https://publications.iom.int/system/files/pdf/iomdataprotection_web.pdf\"><u>https://publications.iom.int/system/<br>files/pdf/iomdataprotection_web.pdf</u></a></p>  <h3>Who has access to these data?</h3> <p>Except for the purposes for which you accepted to provide your personal data, IOM will not disclose your information or your account in the application to any third party, without your prior informed consent. You can read more about our data sharing policy by viewing the IOM Data Protection Principles, available <a href=\"https://www.iom.int/data-protection\" target=\"_blank\" onclick='window.open(\"https://www.iom.int/data-protection\"); return false;'><u>here</u></a><br></br>  Access to your personal data will be limited to IOM staff members dedicated to managing the application. All IOM staff members must adhere to the IOM Data Protection Principles and are strictly bound by confidentiality obligations.<br></br>    Your data will be treated as confidential information.</p>  <h3>What are your rights and how can you manage your data?</h3> <p> You have the right and responsibility to update all personal data you have supplied to the application. You may change your personal data at any time. For that you will need to contact IOM Medical staff and inform about any change in personal data.<br></br>  You can access your personal data in the application at any time by logging in and checking your profile. You can also view your notifications history and vaccination documentation.</p>  <h3>How long will we keep your data for?</h3> <p> Your data will be retained in accordance with IOM data retention policy, which is currently no fewer than 7 years following collection.</p>  <h3>What laws and regulations govern the processing of your data?</h3> <p> All your data is processed in accordance with the IOM Data Protection Principles. IOM reserves the right to change this Privacy Policy at any time. Whenever changes are made, you will be notified through the application and will need to agree in order to continue using it.</p>  <h3>Who to contact if you have questions or complaints?</h3> <p>For any questions in relation to your personal data gathered through the application, you may contact: <a href=\"vaccineapp@iom.int\"><u>vaccineapp@iom.int</u></a></p>  <h3>  2. GENERAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS</h3> <p>  PLEASE READ THESE TERMS CAREFULLY. THE ACCESS TO OR USE OF THE APPLICATION IMPLIES THAT YOU HAVE READ, UNDERSTOOD AND ACCEPTED ALL OF THEM WITHOUT RESERVATION.</p>  <h3>1. Use of the Vaccination Application</h3>  <p>You agree to the following obligations: <br>  ● Not to register if you are under the age of 18;<br>  ●   Not to misrepresent your relationship to another user;<br>  ●   Not to use the application to act in an unlawful, obscene, discriminatory or abusive manner or promote such actions;<br> ●   Not to sell, rent, trade or otherwise monetize any feature of the application or any information accessed through the application; <br> ●   Not to use the application to violate the intellectual property rights of other persons or entities;<br>  ●   Not to use the application to infringe any rights relating to personal data, privacy or protection of the image of any natural person and/or the reputation of a third party by means of the application;<br> ●   Not to use bots, scripts or any other automated method to access and collect information on the application;<br> ●   Not to override any feature of the application. In the event of unfulfillment by the user, the IOM reserves the right to take appropriate legal actions, as well as the right to restrict access to the application</p>  <h3>2. Denying Access </h3> <p>IOM reserves the right to deny, at its sole discretion, any user access to the application or any portion thereof without notice.</p>  <h3>3. Disclaimer</h3>  <p>The content in the application is provided on an \"as is\" basis, without warranty of any kind. IOM specifically does not make any warranties as to the appropriateness, quality, timeliness, accuracy or completeness of the information and services offered through the application. While IOM cannot guarantee that there are no errors in the information provided, it does endeavor to correct errors that are drawn to its attention. The content of this application does not replace the personalized care made by healthcare professionals.</p>  <h3>4. Geographic Names</h3>  <p>While IOM follows the criteria of the United Nations in the geographic names and related data, the information shown in the application is not warranted to be error free.</p>  <h3>5. Bugs, Viruses and other Malware</h3> <p>While IOM makes every effort to ensure the materials available on the application are free of any software virus, it cannot guarantee that they are free from any or all software viruses. IOM is not responsible for any loss or damage caused by software and related codes, including viruses and worms.</p>  <h3>6. Links</h3> <p>At no point, the setting-up of links will imply any relationship or collaboration with, or support by IOM. Particularly, it is not permitted to set-up a link that, fraudulently, may lead to or establish any type of relationship with IOM.</p>  <h3>7. Data Protection</h3> <p>IOM informs you and any third parties whose personal data are processed by the application about its Privacy Policy, which is available above  <a href=\"#Privacy_Policy\"><u>Privacy Policy</u></a></p>  <h3>8. Security Measures</h3> <p>The application implements a series of technologies and security measures in order to safeguard the information maintained by IOM from misuse, unauthorized access or disclosure, alteration or loss. Although IOM applies reasonable means to ensure that the information you provide is not used by third parties for purposes other than those for which you accepted to provide it, IOM cannot guarantee that unauthorized third parties will never be able to defeat security measures or use your personal data for improper purposes. You should be aware that no transmission of information via the internet is ever totally secure. The setting-up of your account and the transmission of any information, including personal data, is at your own risk.</p>  <h3>9. Intellectual Property</h3> <p>9.1 IOM grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable and free license only for private and personal use of the application. This license will have a duration equal to that of the legal relationship established in these General Terms and Conditions. 9.2 All intellectual property rights relating to IOM-owned materials provided through the application shall remain vested in IOM, unless otherwise stated. IOM has the copyright of all materials provided through the application, unless otherwise stated. The materials may be viewed, downloaded, and printed for non-commercial use only, without any right to sell, resell, or create derivative works therefrom. Particularly, and included but not limited to, the user may not use, access, copy, reproduce, transform or create derivative works, decompile, decode, perform reverse engineering, transfer, transmit, rent, distribute, license, sublicense, sell or trade with the application and its contents or rights, or have the application in any other way without previous, express and written authorization of IOM. Permission to use materials which are not owned by IOM must be requested from the copyright owner.</p>  <h3>10. Liability</h3> <p>You understand the risks of transmission of information via the internet and accept that the setting-up and use of the application is at your own risk. You release, discharge and agree to hold harmless IOM, its officers, employees and agents from any liability or damage caused, directly or indirectly, to you, your family or relatives in connection with the use of the application.</p>  <h3>11. Contact <p>If you have any questions or concerns about the Privacy Policy and/or General Terms and Conditions or if you would like to report any incident with the system, you may contact <a href=\"vaccineapp@iom.int\">vaccineapp@iom.int</a> or go directly to the application feedback feature. IOM attempts to respond to messages directed at the organization. However, IOM is under no obligation to respond to any or all such messages.</p>  <h3>12. Notification of Changes</h3> <p>IOM reserves the right to change the General Terms and Conditions and/or Privacy Policy when IOM deems it appropriate, or in order to adapt them to future legislative and technological changes, which will be informed to you through the application. IOM will post changes to the General Terms and Conditions and/or Privacy Policy in the application only.</p>  <h3>13. Privileges and Immunities</h3> <p>Nothing in or relating to these General Terms and Conditions shall be deemed a waiver, express or implied, of any of the privileges and immunities of the IOM as an intergovernmental organization.</p>  <h3>14. Termination</h3> <p>The IOM reserves the exclusive right and discretion to limit, alter, suspend, or terminate the application without notice, in whole or in part, at any time without giving any reason or explanation and without incurring any liability.</p>";
